# Milestone: v0.10.2-reactive (W6, activated post W4-merge)
# Covers: TAG_STOP wakes a sleeping strand mid-sleep.
# defer-to: W4-merge-followup (Tag.new() + .stop() not yet in integration branch)
#
# When W4 (Tag.new + OP_TAG_STOP + script .stop()) merges into
# integration/v0.10.2-reactive, this fixture can be un-deferred:
#   1. Remove this comment block.
#   2. Add expected output lines.
#   3. Confirm PASS on the integration branch.
#
# Mechanism: TAG_STOP on a sleeping strand calls sched_strand_unblock(s)
# via urbi_tag_stop's member_strands walk (src/runtime/uunwind.c line ~542).
# sched_strand_unblock removes the strand from the sleep queue and makes it
# runnable; the strand resumes in UEXEC_TAG_STOP state.
#
# Verified at v0.10.2 W6 dispatch: urbi_tag_stop DOES call
# sched_strand_unblock for WAITING strands, which removes from sleep_q via
# sched_strand_unbind_from_sleep_queue (src/sched/usched_cooperative.c
# sched_strand_unblock at line ~293). No additional change needed for W6.
#
# Once W4 is merged, implement:
#
#   var t = Tag.new("sleeper")
#   Realm.caught = false
#   t: { try { sleep(500ms) } catch (e) { Realm.caught = true } }
#   sleep(50ms)   -- give the sleeper time to enter sleep queue
#   t.stop()
#   sleep(50ms)   -- give the unwind time to deposit
#   Realm.caught
#   [00000000] nil
#   ...
#   [N] true
